# JarvOS continuity — secrets manifest template.
#
# jarvos-sync copies these lines into the profile repo's `secrets.manifest` and
# appends anything it discovered by NAME while capturing (environment variables
# referenced by synced dotfiles, denied paths that exist on the source box).
#
# The manifest is a shopping list, never a container. No value from any of these
# ever enters the repo, the staging tree, or a log line.
#
# Format:  <where it goes> | <what it is> | <how to get it back>

~/.secrets/.env.central | central variable vault (bootstrap + legacy secrets) | copy from your vault / password manager, or re-run its bootstrap
~/.ssh/ | SSH private keys and known_hosts | regenerate per machine (ssh-keygen -t ed25519) and re-register the public key with your forges
~/.gnupg/ | GPG keyring | export from the old machine (gpg --export-secret-keys) or restore from your vault
~/.claude/.credentials.json | Claude Code session credentials | re-authenticate: run `claude` and log in
~/.config/gh/hosts.yml | GitHub CLI token | re-authenticate: `gh auth login`
~/.aws/credentials | AWS credentials | re-authenticate: `aws configure` or SSO login
~/.docker/config.json | container registry logins | `docker login <registry>`
~/.netrc | machine logins for curl/git | recreate from your vault as needed
